{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["The sense of <b>וַיַּעֲבֹר ה' עַל פָּנָיו</b> is that He fulfilled \"I will cause all My goodness to pass before you.\"" "<b>וַיִּקְרָא ה' ה' אֵל</b> — these three words are holy Names, and the Sages call them attributes (Rosh Hashanah 17a), for they are the attribute of the Master of repentance, the attribute of His mercy, and the attribute of His goodness, and the unique Name is not multiplied in them. Now, the attributes that are invoked upon a person are ten attributes — רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן and so forth — and all of them are attributes from one perspective, while from another perspective the three are essential Names and the ten are attributes. And the attributes are predicated of the Names, for רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן וְאֶרֶךְ אַפַּיִם belong to El Elyon; therefore it does not say מְרַחֵם וְחוֹנֵן וּמַאֲרִיךְ אַפַּיִם, because the form is that of a noun (שֵׁם פָּעוּל) for these attributes." "<b>וְרַב חֶסֶד וֶאֱמֶת נֹצֵר חֶסֶד לָאֲלָפִים</b> — in the attribute of mercy, for He multiplies kindness over His might and power, and the truth is in His mercies; and נֹצֵר חֶסֶד לָאֲלָפִים, for \"He has remembered His kindness and His faithfulness to the house of Israel\" (Psalms 98:3). Or נֹצֵר, meaning \"causes to sprout,\" from \"and a shoot (וְנֵצֶר) from his roots shall bear fruit\" (Isaiah 11:1). And in His goodness He is <b>נֹשֵׂא עָוֹן וָפֶשַׁע וְחַטָּאָה</b>, in the sense of \"I have made, and I will bear\" (Isaiah 46:4). <b>וְנַקֵּה לֹא יְנַקֶּה</b> and <b>פּוֹקֵד עֲוֹן אָבוֹת עַל בָּנִים</b> — the explanation pertains to bearing (נְשִׂיאוּת), and it is called an attribute (מִדָּה), for He absolves him in that visitation; and because the bearing is not equal for עָוֹן, וָפֶשַׁע, and חַטָּאָה, but rather each has its own distinct meaning, each is called one attribute:" "Now Moses bowed down to the Name that passed before him and asked that He go always in their midst, and pardon their iniquity and their sin in all that they do, and give them the Land as an inheritance. And he did not say וְלִפְשָׁעֵינוּ, for it is not possible to forgive transgressions (פְּשָׁעִים), which are acts of rebellion, but only that He bear them and not bring shame upon them through them. And let it not be hidden from you why these two Names were written with אָלֶ״ף דָּלֶ״״ד, and because of this He said <b>הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי כּוֹרֵת בְּרִית</b> through <b>אֶת מַעֲשֵׂה ה' כִּי נוֹרָא הוּא</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {3 "The reference to two Names written with אָלֶ״ף דָּלֶ״״ד likely alludes to יהוה and אלהים (or possibly אדני) in kabbalistic juxtaposition; left cryptic per the way of truth."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:33.946450690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}